Jukka Lahtinen wrote:
> Rodan <parkercoons@gmail.com> writes:
>
>> Meaning that there's no limit to how many gifts you can receive? They
>> just become increasingly unlikely?
>
> Essentially so, until you have received all the possible artifacts.

Not counting the Quest artifacts in any of the discussion below, only
the regular weapon artifacts.

The first gift is always co-aligned so for a neutral it is taken from
the list Cleaver, Giantslayer, Magicbane, Mjollnir, Vorpal Blade.  There
is only one junk artifact in that list and two of the five are
ascendable artifact weapons.  The first gift is also filtered for race
but that only matters for elven or orcish chaotic characters.

The second and subsequent gift also includes the list of non-aligned
artifacts so the list also includes Dragonbane, Fire Brand, Frost Brand,
Orgesmasher, Trollsbane and Werebane.  The two Brands are some of the
most powerful artifact weapons in the game and are decidedly not junk. 
Some players altar dance specifically in an attempt to get one of the
Banes.

> After that there's a limit, because there will be no more artifacts to
> receive.

That's true for gifts but there are other ways to get artifacts.  There
are two that the player can make - There is a strategy for when to do
so. There are two that can appear in the inventory of a few type As.
There is one that can appear in the inventory of purple Ls. Any
artifact but Excalibur can appear randomly on the floor - Some games
see an artifact in a shop. Any artifact that does not already exist
can appear from a bones file.


